WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.444 --> 00:00:14.500
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:17.973
[fzzt]

00:00:17.973 --> 00:00:20.734
I am ready. Bestow your
knowledge upon--

00:00:21.342 --> 00:00:23.528
Wait, this is that stupid room again!

00:00:23.528 --> 00:00:24.436
DAMMIT!

00:00:24.436 --> 00:00:26.265
WHY IS THIS SO SPECIAL?!

00:00:26.265 --> 00:00:30.188
WHAT'S THE POINT OF TELEPORTERS IF YOU
CAN ONLY TELEPORT INTO THE NEXT ROOM?!

00:00:30.188 --> 00:00:31.349
IT CAN'T BE A PROTOTYPE!

00:00:31.349 --> 00:00:34.620
YOU DON'T MAKE NINE FUCKING
PROTOTYPES WITH THE SAME DESIGN FLAW!

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:35.889
I'm leaving!

00:00:35.889 --> 00:00:38.994
No... there's nothing
here. I know that.

00:00:38.994 --> 00:00:41.315
All right, there's some
I haven't tried.

00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:43.028
Merry-go-round techno bullshit...

00:00:43.028 --> 00:00:44.114
[fzzt]

00:00:44.114 --> 00:00:46.889
So, wait, how does
this know to teleport me?

00:00:46.889 --> 00:00:49.048
Does it detect organic compounds?

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:52.488
But that wouldn't make sense, then
I'd be naked like in the Terminator.

00:00:52.488 --> 00:00:53.847
The suit wouldn't make it.

00:00:53.847 --> 00:00:54.756
[fzzt]

00:00:54.756 --> 00:00:57.932
I mean, maybe the suit has
some carbon fiber... I don't know.

00:00:57.932 --> 00:00:59.630
But the metal wouldn't pass.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:04.062
Maybe it scans everything that's not
the ground or air and teleports that?

00:01:04.062 --> 00:01:06.635
But then wouldn't dust
pile up at the exit?

00:01:06.635 --> 00:01:07.387
[fzzt]

00:01:07.387 --> 00:01:09.975
Yeah, what am I
talking about? "Scanners"...

00:01:09.975 --> 00:01:13.958
Okay, I haven't tried THIS one.
I guess I could climb the fence.

00:01:13.958 --> 00:01:14.771
Yah!

00:01:14.771 --> 00:01:19.751
All right, I've already tried "8".
The big teleporters are exactly the same.

00:01:19.751 --> 00:01:22.000
This one looks kind of fucked up.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.257
Okay, I'll try "7", then if that
doesn't work, I'll climb the fence.

00:01:26.257 --> 00:01:28.727
Yeah, "scanners"... We have
don't have computers that would

00:01:28.727 --> 00:01:32.044
even come CLOSE to scanning all
the atoms in a human body.

00:01:32.044 --> 00:01:35.139
One fantasy at a time.
Because that's what this is.

00:01:35.139 --> 00:01:37.609
There's just no explanation for anything.

00:01:37.609 --> 00:01:42.363
Ah, now I'm going to wait so that
other green ball doesn't kill me.

00:01:42.363 --> 00:01:43.102
Daaaah?

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.653
[fzzt]

00:01:44.653 --> 00:01:46.668
Oh. I overprepared.

00:01:46.668 --> 00:01:48.484
It's been a long since I've done that,

00:01:48.484 --> 00:01:52.400
since every moment has been one
worst case scenario after another.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.233
Looks like it still is.

00:01:54.233 --> 00:01:55.610
What am I looking at?

00:01:55.610 --> 00:02:00.619
Obviously, no one was ever meant to be
in this room or walk in it, but here I am.

00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:02.046
[Geiger counter ticking]
Is this a reactor?

00:02:02.046 --> 00:02:03.337
[Geiger counter ticking]
The Geiger counter's not ticking

00:02:03.337 --> 00:02:06.277
[Geiger counter ticking]
quite that high, but, shit...

00:02:06.277 --> 00:02:08.984
Okay, I guess... fuck...

00:02:08.984 --> 00:02:13.163
I think there's a passageway
on the other end, maybe...

00:02:13.163 --> 00:02:15.040
Yeah, this is helpful!

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.388
All right, well, I haven't had enough
spinning today, so this is perfect.

00:02:19.388 --> 00:02:21.093
Just what I was hoping for.

00:02:21.093 --> 00:02:22.033
Okay, let's go.

00:02:22.676 --> 00:02:24.699
Wait, shit!  No, noNONONO!

00:02:24.699 --> 00:02:27.915
It's too bad there's nobody
shooting at me while I'm doing this!

00:02:27.915 --> 00:02:30.382
That would really
complete the experience!

00:02:30.382 --> 00:02:32.721
Okay, jump... Frogger from hell...

00:02:32.721 --> 00:02:34.297
That's good... jump!

00:02:34.297 --> 00:02:35.423
WAAAAAH!

00:02:35.423 --> 00:02:37.619
[exhaling]

00:02:37.619 --> 00:02:38.814
Button!

00:02:38.814 --> 00:02:40.164
What did that do?

00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:43.163
Jesus Christ, that looks
like a crematorium furnace.

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:45.145
Well, the rad levels are holding steady

00:02:45.145 --> 00:02:48.003
so whatever's in there isn't any
worse than what's already here.

00:02:48.003 --> 00:02:50.934
Maybe this reactor is
powered by human souls.

00:02:52.281 --> 00:02:52.915
Yah!

00:02:52.915 --> 00:02:55.392
That would explain why
I've barely seen anyone.

00:02:55.392 --> 00:02:59.979
I still have doubts about how much
"science" is involved with these teleporters.

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:00.793
Dah...

00:03:00.793 --> 00:03:02.696
What's that Arthur C. Clarke quote?

00:03:02.696 --> 00:03:06.925
"Any sufficiently advanced technology
is indistinguishable from magic"?

00:03:06.925 --> 00:03:09.781
Well, that doesn't RULE OUT magic!

00:03:09.781 --> 00:03:11.711
Button 1! Hop to it!

00:03:11.711 --> 00:03:13.797
Oh, yeah! That was smooth!

00:03:13.797 --> 00:03:17.605
Okay, so the plan is I crawl in
there and somehow not die.

00:03:17.605 --> 00:03:19.701
If I start to die, then I'll stop.

00:03:20.576 --> 00:03:21.980
Yeah, I don't feel any heat.

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.100
[fzzt]

00:03:24.681 --> 00:03:27.067
Oh, I'm here. I could've just--

00:03:27.929 --> 00:03:31.661
All right. No sense in
lamenting the past.

00:03:31.661 --> 00:03:32.949
So, do I take this?

00:03:32.949 --> 00:03:35.968
It probably just leads back to
that same room, but...

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:40.375
Wow! This door isn't locked!

00:03:40.375 --> 00:03:42.398
I didn't think that was possible.

00:03:42.398 --> 00:03:46.046
I was starting to suspect these
were all welded pieces of steel,

00:03:46.046 --> 00:03:49.670
that were stolen from the
supports to the building, apparently.

00:03:49.670 --> 00:03:52.354
Is this a real door? We will never know.

00:03:52.354 --> 00:03:53.853
Ah, my entourage.

00:03:53.853 --> 00:03:54.834
You're late!

00:03:55.904 --> 00:03:58.400
I have no tolerance for tardiness!

00:03:58.949 --> 00:04:03.124
Unless it's me, but you
are SO obviously not me.

00:04:03.124 --> 00:04:05.148
Sleeping on the job, huh?

00:04:05.148 --> 00:04:07.563
Well, I'm not your boss. Carry on.

00:04:08.238 --> 00:04:11.674
Yeah, I can't get over it. These
teleporters still make no sense.

00:04:11.674 --> 00:04:14.906
Wouldn't canceling all
momentum stop my brain, too?

00:04:14.906 --> 00:04:17.970
I can maybe buy that this was a
scientific breakthrough,

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.656
but this is such a fundamental
change in our understanding,

00:04:20.656 --> 00:04:23.225
[metal groaning]
it would take a series of breakthroughs.

00:04:23.225 --> 00:04:23.934
Huh.

00:04:24.678 --> 00:04:27.831
No, I think magic might
actually have a case here.

00:04:27.831 --> 00:04:29.876
I mean, there was that
coven that summoned me,

00:04:29.876 --> 00:04:33.567
and I'm pretty sure I saw some
candles, maybe a pentagram.

00:04:34.128 --> 00:04:35.534
Oh, shit, he's packing!

00:04:36.366 --> 00:04:37.954
Okay, old man.

00:04:37.954 --> 00:04:40.700
Don't play with fire if you're
not ready to get burned.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.309
You brought this on yourself.

00:04:42.309 --> 00:04:44.351
SCIENTIST: Gordon Freeman,
you finally found us.

00:04:44.351 --> 00:04:44.924
Wait...

00:04:44.924 --> 00:04:47.336
GUARD: So, this is the guy. We
thought you'd never make it.

00:04:47.336 --> 00:04:48.013
Who are you?

00:04:48.013 --> 00:04:51.030
SCIENTIST: This is the supply
depot for our first survey team.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:54.191
SCIENTIST: Quite a few handsome specimens
were collected from the border world,

00:04:54.191 --> 00:04:55.813
SCIENTIST: and brought back this way.

00:04:55.813 --> 00:04:59.950
SCIENTIST: Um, before the survey members
started being collected themselves, that is.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:00.384
Uh...

00:05:00.384 --> 00:05:03.211
SCIENTIST: We suspect there is
an immense portal over there,

00:05:03.211 --> 00:05:07.289
SCIENTIST: created by the intense
concentration of a single powerful being.

00:05:07.289 --> 00:05:08.848
SCIENTIST: You will know it
when you see it.

00:05:08.848 --> 00:05:09.220
What?!

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.230
SCIENTIST: I hate to say this, Gordon,
but you must kill it, if you can.

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:13.074
Whoa, wait a minute...!

00:05:13.074 --> 00:05:14.442
GUARD: Yeah, you'd BETTER kill it.

00:05:14.442 --> 00:05:16.565
DON'T YOU TALK TO ME LIKE THAT, YOU--

00:05:16.565 --> 00:05:18.475
SCIENTIST: 'course, you owe us
nothing, Mr. Freeman.

00:05:18.475 --> 00:05:20.198
DAMN STRAIGHT!

00:05:20.198 --> 00:05:22.257
SCIENTIST: You know as much
about these creatures as anyone.

00:05:22.257 --> 00:05:23.396
You just have to shoot 'em.

00:05:23.396 --> 00:05:26.736
GUARD: --if you don't wipe it out, there
won't be much for you to come home to.

00:05:26.736 --> 00:05:28.593
What about YOU, tough guy?

00:05:28.593 --> 00:05:30.436
SCIENTIST: So, if you're willing,

00:05:30.436 --> 00:05:33.286
SCIENTIST: my colleague is waiting for
you at the main portal controls.

00:05:33.286 --> 00:05:35.888
SCIENTIST: He will open the gates
for you, Mr. Freeman. Do hurry.

00:05:35.888 --> 00:05:36.713
Okay, listen--

00:05:36.713 --> 00:05:37.745
GUARD: Don't forget to gear up.

00:05:37.745 --> 00:05:38.222
[sighs]

00:05:38.222 --> 00:05:40.091
GUARD: And I'll cover you while you're
waiting for that portal to warm up.

00:05:40.091 --> 00:05:41.135
Yeah, whatever.

00:05:41.135 --> 00:05:43.968
Listen, this portal thing sounds
great, but I need you to--

00:05:44.658 --> 00:05:46.274
Are you serious?

00:05:46.274 --> 00:05:49.063
Are you walking away
as I'm talking to--

00:05:49.063 --> 00:05:51.677
Hey, meatloaf. Tell your
friend with Asperger's,

00:05:51.677 --> 00:05:54.636
I need to get teleported
to Massachusetts.

00:05:54.636 --> 00:05:56.000
Or anywhere outside of--

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:56.604
SCIENTIST: This, Mr. Freeman,

00:05:56.604 --> 00:05:58.008
Oh, what now?
SCIENTIST: is the long jump module.

00:05:58.008 --> 00:06:01.497
SCIENTIST: created expressly for
navigation in the world beyond.

00:06:01.497 --> 00:06:04.146
SCIENTIST: I certainly hope you
received long jump training,

00:06:04.146 --> 00:06:07.006
SCIENTIST: because once
you're in Xen, you will need it.

00:06:07.006 --> 00:06:09.194
SCIENTIST: I would advise you to
practice before crossing over.

00:06:09.194 --> 00:06:11.830
Zen and the Art of Long Jumping, huh?

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.139
Didn't take you for a Zen guy.

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:16.400
This thing would've been great YESTERDAY!

00:06:17.566 --> 00:06:20.133
Oh, yeah! I missed this!

00:06:21.198 --> 00:06:23.559
Man, I could tackle you so hard.

00:06:23.559 --> 00:06:25.284
All right, I'll deal with you later.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:29.176
First thing's first. I'm seeing
a lot of ammo lying around,

00:06:29.176 --> 00:06:31.973
so I'm going to assume
you laid it out here for me.

00:06:31.973 --> 00:06:34.410
Thanks. That's very
forward-thinking of you.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:38.481
I'm not even going to ask why a
lab has so many small arms in here.

00:06:38.481 --> 00:06:39.767
I'm cool like that.

00:06:40.655 --> 00:06:44.176
And, hey, I can't carry two,
but I'll take the rocket out.

00:06:44.176 --> 00:06:45.612
Yeah, this is good.

00:06:45.612 --> 00:06:47.595
It's just as well I'm
coming through here;

00:06:47.595 --> 00:06:50.700
you two would only hurt yourself
with these given enough time.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:53.711
Hey, it's another one of those
Ghostbuster props.

00:06:53.711 --> 00:06:54.982
Why not?

00:06:54.982 --> 00:06:55.801
Does it work?

00:06:57.241 --> 00:06:58.500
Yeah, looks good.

00:06:59.316 --> 00:07:01.884
Well, you guys are
just full of goodies.

00:07:01.884 --> 00:07:03.386
More shells.

00:07:03.386 --> 00:07:04.701
What is that?

00:07:04.701 --> 00:07:07.819
Well, I'm not touching THAT
but I'll take more explosives.

00:07:07.819 --> 00:07:11.642
Explosives keep my options open
in a way nothing else can.

00:07:11.642 --> 00:07:15.167
Now, what I REALLY need...
is a wheelbarrow.

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:16.968
But...

00:07:18.335 --> 00:07:20.815
I'll just take every
single thing I can carry.

00:07:20.815 --> 00:07:23.233
But that's the least this
company can do for me,

00:07:23.233 --> 00:07:26.354
and it WILL do more, but one
step at a time here.

00:07:27.298 --> 00:07:28.319
What's this?

00:07:29.368 --> 00:07:31.987
Oh, these are explosives!

00:07:31.987 --> 00:07:36.279
Wow, this is the most hardcore
lab storage I've seen in my life.

00:07:36.279 --> 00:07:37.033
Hello!

00:07:37.641 --> 00:07:39.577
What's this, a prototype weapon?

00:07:39.577 --> 00:07:41.250
I hope it's a weapon.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.231
Let's see.

00:07:42.231 --> 00:07:43.000
There's a trigger.

00:07:43.848 --> 00:07:45.067
Yeah, it's doing something.

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:47.634
Hey, there's a throttle.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:53.177
WOW! That kicks like a shotgun!
This'd better be a weapon.

00:07:53.177 --> 00:07:55.063
I really should try this
on a live target,

00:07:55.063 --> 00:07:59.025
but there's going to be nothing
but drama if I shoot this guy in the leg.

00:07:59.025 --> 00:08:01.734
Okay, I think I'm getting
close to my limit.

00:08:01.734 --> 00:08:05.935
I can grab a couple things, but if I carry
much more, I'm going to need some duct tape.

00:08:05.935 --> 00:08:08.367
All right, Tickle Me Bald Guy,
we've gotta talk.

00:08:08.729 --> 00:08:10.801
Oh, he's bowing. Okay...

00:08:10.801 --> 00:08:15.249
Hey, forget this alien stuff. You need to
teleport me to Massachusetts, all right?

00:08:15.249 --> 00:08:16.476
Massachusetts.

00:08:16.476 --> 00:08:18.772
That's simple enough, I think
you can remember it.

00:08:18.772 --> 00:08:19.729
[machine buzzing]
What the hell?

00:08:19.729 --> 00:08:22.450
Heh, yeah, I guess I am
carrying some contraband.

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.811
Man, it's too bad these
teleporters aren't the duplicating kind,

00:08:25.811 --> 00:08:28.414
then we can just tell it to not
destroy me on this end,

00:08:28.414 --> 00:08:30.429
and I can create copies of myself.

00:08:30.429 --> 00:08:33.509
Now, the conventional wisdom is
if you see a clone of yourself,

00:08:33.509 --> 00:08:36.985
you should try to kill it, but I
think that's the view of a small mind.

00:08:36.985 --> 00:08:37.659
SCIENTIST: Hello, Freeman!

00:08:37.659 --> 00:08:39.129
Dah!
SCIENTIST: I'm up here!

00:08:39.129 --> 00:08:41.460
SCIENTIST: Practice your long
jump if you must, but hurry up!

00:08:41.460 --> 00:08:44.634
All right, all right. I'm
coming, just hold on.

00:08:46.036 --> 00:08:46.693
Hah!

00:08:46.693 --> 00:08:51.172
Y'know, a ladder wouldn't kill you;
this catwalk has poor support as it is.

00:08:51.172 --> 00:08:52.974
There's too much stress on the beam.

00:08:52.974 --> 00:08:55.459
Actually, hold on. Is there an exit here?

00:08:55.459 --> 00:08:59.829
Like, is there a snack machine in the
back or something? Because I could use that.

00:08:59.829 --> 00:09:01.223
No...

00:09:01.223 --> 00:09:02.614
Hey, I don't know what they told you,

00:09:02.614 --> 00:09:05.326
but I need you to teleport
me to Massachusetts.

00:09:05.326 --> 00:09:07.598
If you can't swing that, just
get me to the nearest city

00:09:07.598 --> 00:09:10.106
like Los Alamos or
Santa Fe would be fine.

00:09:10.106 --> 00:09:12.138
I should be able to hijack
a ride, no problem.

00:09:12.138 --> 00:09:14.288
SCIENTIST: All right, I can open
the portal now.

00:09:14.288 --> 00:09:18.268
SCIENTIST: The process is complicated and
once it's begun, I must not be interrupted

00:09:18.268 --> 00:09:20.525
SCIENTIST: or I will have to
start all over again.

00:09:20.525 --> 00:09:23.407
SCIENTIST: DON'T enter the beam
until I give the okay. Understood?

00:09:23.407 --> 00:09:23.931
Yeah.

00:09:23.931 --> 00:09:24.622
SCIENTIST: I will begin.

00:09:24.622 --> 00:09:27.314
I'll get out of your hair.
Just don't screw up.

00:09:27.314 --> 00:09:29.920
Man, if the teleporter COULD
make a copy of me,

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.945
I should have a plan how to
unite myselves in the future,

00:09:32.945 --> 00:09:36.573
so I need to have a plan NOW
before I make the jump, just in case.

00:09:36.573 --> 00:09:39.930
I guess... I'll leave contact info
where I buried the gold. That'll work.

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:40.737
SCIENTIST: Oh dear!

00:09:40.737 --> 00:09:41.634
What is it?

00:09:42.436 --> 00:09:43.500
AH! Shit.

00:09:46.714 --> 00:09:47.602
AH!

00:09:47.602 --> 00:09:49.901
WHAT IS THAT?!
THEY CAN FLY NOW?!

00:09:50.539 --> 00:09:50.868
AH!

00:09:51.528 --> 00:09:53.767
HEY, YOU'VE GOT A FEW BUGS IN THE SYSTEM!

00:09:54.677 --> 00:09:56.539
I MEAN, A LOT OF BUGS!

00:09:56.539 --> 00:09:58.033
HOW ABOUT FIXING THAT?!

00:09:59.095 --> 00:10:02.541
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU'RE DOING,
BUT YOU'RE DOING IT WRONG!

00:10:02.541 --> 00:10:03.133
Christ...

00:10:06.818 --> 00:10:10.100
I'M PUTTING A LOT MORE TRUST IN
YOU THAN I WANT TO BE RIGHT NOW!

00:10:10.692 --> 00:10:11.400
Jesus!

00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:17.027
THEY KEEP COMING! YOU'VE HIT A NEST!

00:10:17.027 --> 00:10:18.616
SCIENTIST: [inaudible]

00:10:18.616 --> 00:10:19.267
WHAT?!

00:10:19.966 --> 00:10:21.167
AAH! AH!

00:10:22.442 --> 00:10:24.100
YOU NEED ME TO COME UP THERE?

00:10:25.477 --> 00:10:27.067
BECAUSE THIS ISN'T WORKING!

00:10:27.864 --> 00:10:29.934
SHUT IT DOWN! JUST SHUT IT DOWN!

00:10:30.854 --> 00:10:32.553
YOU NEED TO START OVER!

00:10:32.553 --> 00:10:33.592
SCIENTIST: [inaudible]

00:10:33.592 --> 00:10:35.200
I CAN'T HEAR YOU!

00:10:36.513 --> 00:10:38.486
HEY, IT'S DOING SOMETHING NOW!

00:10:38.486 --> 00:10:39.667
SHOULD I GO-- WAAAAAAAAH!

00:10:40.584 --> 00:10:43.868
I'M NOT WAITING; I'M GOING TO GO!
DON'T FUCK ME ON THIS!

00:10:44.351 --> 00:10:46.801
WAAAAAAAAAAAAAGH! NO!

00:10:48.977 --> 00:10:49.534
Christ...

00:10:50.885 --> 00:10:52.167
THIS IS SO FUCKED!

00:10:52.167 --> 00:10:54.037
[screaming]
WHAT?!

00:10:54.037 --> 00:10:54.834
[fzzt]

00:11:00.271 --> 00:11:00.634
[fzzt]

00:11:07.019 --> 00:11:09.595
[fzzt]
YAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA--

00:11:09.595 --> 00:11:10.033
[fzzt]

